meta {
  name: Gated site — remote sign-in screencast (SSE)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/connectors/{{scrapeConnector}}/browser/session/frames
}

docs {
  Only relevant when the sign-in started via request 7 came back with `mode: "remote"` —
  i.e. QuickJoiner has no display of its own (Docker/cloud), so it runs the login page
  headless and streams it here as polled JPEG frames instead of opening a window.

  Server-Sent Events: one `meta` event first (`{width, height}` — the actual frame size,
  so a viewer never hardcodes a viewport), then a `frame` event roughly every 200ms
  (`{data: "<base64 jpeg>"}`), ending with `done`. 404 if no remote sign-in is running for
  this connector.

  A Bruno request can't drive input/canvas rendering — this call is here mainly to confirm
  the stream opens; see the QuickJoiner web UI's RemoteBrowserModal for the actual viewer.
}
